    {
      "id": "claim_ac3021edc3fb4f8d9b30ba295950431c",
      "statement": "A cached vp run strips the environment and a var can only be declared on a task: workshop-frontend's build is a task declaring env ['VITE_*'] so the flags are forwarded and folded into the fingerprint (a changed value is a reported cache miss rather than a stale replay); a task may not share a name with a script.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/vite.config.ts#L14-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0a61d9314783caddcc3dde36d149fd068f21ff546bbe7e16577b71f8882d2c6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_437b9508269641f3b93dc1008d3e3fa3",
      "statement": "vp declines to cache a task that reads a path it also writes, so the frontend build excludes its own dist/ (package-relative, because typed-storage emits to dist and a workspace-wide exclusion would drop a real input) and excludes .wrangler/** workspace-wide because wrangler's randomly-named scratch bundles reach past the owning package.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/vite.config.ts#L15-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7fd9508c7850fde627dc6ecbaf7417157b056a586e8c9ddcf7df17c4724bbbcd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df552ef92b064cb5ba5f39518c575952",
      "statement": "The gatekeeper configurator build is a task so VITE_FRONTEND_ERROR_REPORTING is passed through and fingerprinted, with an uncached clean:error-reporting-artifacts dependency first (a cache hit restores archived outputs without deleting, so a disabled-reporting deploy could otherwise keep an enabled build's sourcemaps); deploy reaches it via vp run --no-cache build:configurator because deploys never trust the fingerprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gatekeeper-configurator-vite-config.ts#L7-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8fc450ed973e2c677e045c7c87ad4ba4e40349deeb541fca7a88eb9cc1c4d3a4:"
